      },
      "motion": "slow_push_in",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "Livyatan's teeth are the reason this animal is famous. Its nickname, \"megatooth whale,\" comes from them."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s04_02",
      "scene": 4,
      "scene_title": "Teeth",
      "start_sec": 116.689,
      "end_sec": 131.485,
      "duration_sec": 14.796,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s04_02.jpg",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s04_02.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 14.446,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "~30 cm (1 ft)",
      "narration": "The largest teeth are estimated at around 30 centimeters, about a foot long. These weren't small, flat teeth built for grinding. They were long, conical, and sharp, the kind of teeth you'd expect on something that grabs and holds."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s04_03",
      "scene": 4,
      "scene_title": "Teeth",
      "start_sec": 131.485,
      "end_sec": 140.429,
      "duration_sec": 8.944,
      "image": {
        "path": "images/s04_03.jpg",
        "status": "ready"
      },
      "clip": null,
      "audio": {
        "path": "voiceover/s04_03.mp3",
        "status": "ready",
        "duration_sec": 8.594,
        "words": []
      },
      "motion": "none",
      "overlay_text": "",
      "narration": "Think about what that means. Most whales today don't use teeth to catch food at all. They filter tiny animals through baleen plates."
    },
    {
      "shot_id": "s04_04",
      "scene": 4,
      "scene_title": "Teeth",
      "start_sec": 140.429,
      "end_sec": 150.575,
